{"id":"mahabharata-12-009","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":9,"title":"नवमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 9 · Yudhishthira's reply on renunciation","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira answers that the pursuit of kingship has brought only sorrow, and that he longs for the way of the ascetic who has no wealth and no desires. He describes the life of a wandering mendicant who bears all with a quiet mind.","kn":"ರಾಜತ್ವದ ಅನ್ವೇಷಣೆ ದುಃಖವನ್ನೇ ತಂದಿದೆ, ಧನ-ಆಸೆ ಇಲ್ಲದ ತಪಸ್ವಿಯ ಮಾರ್ಗವನ್ನು ತಾನು ಬಯಸುವೆನೆಂದು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಉತ್ತರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಶಾಂತ ಮನಸ್ಸಿನಿಂದ ಎಲ್ಲವನ್ನೂ ಸಹಿಸುವ ಅಲೆಮಾರಿ ಭಿಕ್ಷುವಿನ ಜೀವನವನ್ನು ವರ್ಣಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर उत्तर देते हैं कि राजत्व की खोज ने केवल दुःख दिया है, और वे धन तथा इच्छाओं से रहित तपस्वी का मार्ग चाहते हैं। वे उस घुमक्कड़ भिक्षु के जीवन का वर्णन करते हैं जो शान्त मन से सब सहता है।","te":"రాజ్యాన్వేషణ దుఃఖాన్నే తెచ్చిందని, ధనం కోరికలు లేని తపస్వి మార్గాన్ని కోరుతున్నానని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు బదులిస్తాడు. ప్రశాంత మనసుతో అన్నీ సహించే సంచార భిక్షువు జీవితాన్ని వర్ణిస్తాడు.","ta":"அரசைத் தேடியது துயரையே தந்தது, செல்வமும் ஆசையும் அற்ற துறவியின் வழியை விரும்புகிறேன் என்று யுதிஷ்டிரர் பதிலளிக்கிறார். அமைதியான மனத்துடன் எல்லாவற்றையும் தாங்கும் அலையும் பிக்ஷுவின் வாழ்வை விவரிக்கிறார்.","ml":"രാജത്വത്തിനുവേണ്ടിയുള്ള പരിശ്രമം ദുഃഖം മാത്രമേ നൽകിയിട്ടുള്ളൂവെന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ മറുപടി പറയുന്നു; ധനമോ ആഗ്രഹമോ ഇല്ലാത്ത തപസ്വിയുടെ വഴി അദ്ദേഹം കൊതിക്കുന്നു. സമാധാനമുള്ള മനസ്സോടെ എല്ലാം സഹിക്കുന്ന, അലഞ്ഞുനടക്കുന്ന ഭിക്ഷുവിന്റെ ജീവിതം അദ്ദേഹം വിവരിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.9; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"राजधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Rajadharma Parva (Duties of kings)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"मुहूर्तं तावदेकाग्रो मनःश्रोत्रेऽन्तरात्मनि ।\nधारयित्वापि ते श्रुत्वा रोचतां वचनं मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"For a moment, one-pointed, hold your mind and hearing within your inner self; then, having heard, let my words please you."}},{"n":2,"text":"सार्थगम्यमहं मार्गं न जातु त्वत्कृते पुनः ।\nगच्छेयं तद्गमिष्यामि हित्वा ग्राम्यसुखान्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will never again take, for your sake, a road that people travel together in company. I shall go, giving up the pleasures of village life."}},{"n":3,"text":"क्षेम्यश्चैकाकिना गम्यः पन्थाः कोऽस्तीति पृच्छ माम् ।\nअथ वा नेच्छसि प्रष्टुमपृच्छन्नपि मे शृणु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ask me what safe road can be walked alone. Or, if you do not wish to ask, listen to me anyway."}},{"n":4,"text":"हित्वा ग्राम्यसुखाचारं तप्यमानो महत्तपः ।\nअरण्ये फलमूलाशी चरिष्यामि मृगैः सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Leaving behind the ways of village pleasure and practicing great austerity, I shall wander in the forest, living on fruits and roots, among the deer."}},{"n":5,"text":"जुह्वानोऽग्निं यथाकालमुभौ कालावुपस्पृशन् ।\nकृशः परिमिताहारश्चर्मचीरजटाधरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I shall pour oblations into the fire at the proper times and touch water at both twilights, lean, with measured food, wearing hide, bark and matted hair."}},{"n":6,"text":"शीतवातातपसहः क्षुत्पिपासाश्रमक्षमः ।\nतपसा विधिदृष्टेन शरीरमुपशोषयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Enduring cold, wind and heat, bearing hunger, thirst and toil, I shall wither the body with austerity as the rules prescribe."}},{"n":7,"text":"मनःकर्णसुखा नित्यं शृण्वन्नुच्चावचा गिरः ।\nमुदितानामरण्येषु वसतां मृगपक्षिणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I shall always hear, pleasing to mind and ear, the many cries of the happy beasts and birds that live in the forests."}},{"n":8,"text":"आजिघ्रन्पेशलान्गन्धान्फुल्लानां वृक्षवीरुधाम् ।\nनानारूपान्वने पश्यन्रमणीयान्वनौकसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I shall breathe the sweet scent of flowering trees and creepers and look at the lovely creatures of the forest in their many forms."}},{"n":9,"text":"वानप्रस्थजनस्यापि दर्शनं कुलवासिनः ।\nनाप्रियाण्याचरिष्यामि किं पुनर्ग्रामवासिनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will do nothing unpleasant even to the forest hermits who live there with their families; how much less to villagers."}},{"n":10,"text":"एकान्तशीली विमृशन्पक्वापक्वेन वर्तयन् ।\nपितॄन्देवांश्च वन्येन वाग्भिरद्भिश्च तर्पयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Living apart and reflecting, supporting myself on what is ripe or unripe, I shall satisfy ancestors and gods with forest produce, with words and with water."}},{"n":11,"text":"एवमारण्यशास्त्राणामुग्रमुग्रतरं विधिम् ।\nसेवमानः प्रतीक्षिष्ये देहस्यास्य समापनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Practicing in this way the ever harsher rule of the forest scriptures, I shall wait for the end of this body."}},{"n":12,"text":"अथ वैकोऽहमेकाहमेकैकस्मिन्वनस्पतौ ।\nचरन्भैक्ष्यं मुनिर्मुण्डः क्षपयिष्ये कलेवरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or else, alone, one day at each tree, a shaven sage going about for alms, I shall wear this body away."}},{"n":13,"text":"पांसुभिः समवच्छन्नः शून्यागारप्रतिश्रयः ।\nवृक्षमूलनिकेतो वा त्यक्तसर्वप्रियाप्रियः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Covered with dust, taking shelter in empty houses or at the foot of a tree, giving up all that is pleasing and unpleasing,"}},{"n":14,"text":"न शोचन्न प्रहृष्यंश्च तुल्यनिन्दात्मसंस्तुतिः ।\nनिराशीर्निर्ममो भूत्वा निर्द्वंद्वो निष्परिग्रहः ॥","meaning":{"en":"neither grieving nor rejoicing, treating blame and praise of myself alike, without hope or possessiveness, beyond the pairs of opposites, owning nothing,"}},{"n":15,"text":"आत्मारामः प्रसन्नात्मा जडान्धबधिराकृतिः ।\nअकुर्वाणः परैः कांचित्संविदं जातु केनचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"delighting in the self, with a calm spirit, looking like one who is dull, blind and deaf, never making any agreement with anyone,"}},{"n":16,"text":"जङ्गमाजङ्गमान्सर्वान्नविहिंसंश्चतुर्विधान् ।\nप्रजाः सर्वाः स्वधर्मस्थाः समः प्राणभृतः प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"harming no living thing, moving or unmoving, of the four kinds of beings, and equal toward all creatures, each one abiding in its own nature,"}},{"n":17,"text":"न चाप्यवहसन्कंचिन्न कुर्वन्भ्रुकुटीं क्वचित् ।\nप्रसन्नवदनो नित्यं सर्वेन्द्रियसुसंयतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"not mocking anyone, never knitting my brow, my face serene always and all my senses well restrained,"}},{"n":18,"text":"अपृच्छन्कस्यचिन्मार्गं व्रजन्येनैव केनचित् ।\nन देशं न दिशं कांचिद्गन्तुमिच्छन्विशेषतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"asking no one the way, going along whatever road, not wishing to reach any particular place or direction,"}},{"n":19,"text":"गमने निरपेक्षश्च पश्चादनवलोकयन् ।\nऋजुः प्रणिहितो गच्छंस्त्रसस्थावरवर्जकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"indifferent to the going, not looking back, walking straight and composed, avoiding both moving and unmoving creatures."}},{"n":20,"text":"स्वभावस्तु प्रयात्यग्रे प्रभवन्त्यशनान्यपि ।\nद्वंद्वानि च विरुद्धानि तानि सर्वाण्यचिन्तयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"My nature will go ahead of me and my food will come of itself, and I will give no thought to all the conflicting pairs."}},{"n":21,"text":"अल्पं वास्वादु वा भोज्यं पूर्वालाभेन जातु चित् ।\nअन्येष्वपि चरँल्लाभमलाभे सप्त पूरयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whether the food is little or tasty, if I get none the first time, I will go on to others, and if I get none, I will fill the seven days."}},{"n":22,"text":"विधूमे न्यस्तमुसले व्यङ्गारे भुक्तवज्जने ।\nअतीतपात्रसंचारे काले विगतभिक्षुके ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the smoke has gone and the pestle is laid down, when the embers are out and the people have eaten, when the dishes have stopped going about and the beggars are gone,"}},{"n":23,"text":"एककालं चरन्भैक्ष्यं गृहे द्वे चैव पञ्च च ।\nस्पृहापाशान्विमुच्याहं चरिष्यामि महीमिमाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"going at one time only for alms to two or five houses, I shall wander this earth, freed from the snares of craving."}},{"n":24,"text":"न जिजीविषुवत्किंचिन्न मुमूर्षुवदाचरन् ।\nजीवितं मरणं चैव नाभिनन्दन्न च द्विषन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Acting neither like one who wants to live nor like one who wants to die, neither welcoming nor hating life or death,"}},{"n":25,"text":"वास्यैकं तक्षतो बाहुं चन्दनेनैकमुक्षतः ।\nनाकल्याणं न कल्याणं चिन्तयन्नुभयोस्तयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"thinking neither harm nor good of the man who cuts one arm with an adze nor of the one who anoints the other with sandalwood,"}},{"n":26,"text":"याः काश्चिज्जीवता शक्याः कर्तुमभ्युदयक्रियाः ।\nसर्वास्ताः समभित्यज्य निमेषादिव्यवस्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"renouncing every act that a living man can do for advancement, standing still as though in the blink of an eye,"}},{"n":27,"text":"तेषु नित्यमसक्तश्च त्यक्तसर्वेन्द्रियक्रियः ।\nसुपरित्यक्तसंकल्पः सुनिर्णिक्तात्मकल्मषः ॥","meaning":{"en":"always unattached to them, giving up all activity of the senses, having wholly abandoned willing, and washed clean of the stain of the self,"}},{"n":28,"text":"विमुक्तः सर्वसङ्गेभ्यो व्यतीतः सर्ववागुराः ।\nन वशे कस्यचित्तिष्ठन्सधर्मा मातरिश्वनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"freed of every attachment, past all snares, subject to no one, like the wind in nature,"}},{"n":29,"text":"वीतरागश्चरन्नेवं तुष्टिं प्राप्स्यामि शाश्वतीम् ।\nतृष्णया हि महत्पापमज्ञानादस्मि कारितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"walking thus without passion, I shall gain lasting contentment. For through craving, from ignorance, I have been made to commit great sin."}},{"n":30,"text":"कुशलाकुशलान्येके कृत्वा कर्माणि मानवाः ।\nकार्यकारणसंश्लिष्टं स्वजनं नाम बिभ्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some men do deeds, good and bad, and bear the name of kin, bound up with cause and effect."}},{"n":31,"text":"आयुषोऽन्ते प्रहायेदं क्षीणप्रायं कलेवरम् ।\nप्रतिगृह्णाति तत्पापं कर्तुः कर्मफलं हि तत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"At the end of life they leave this nearly spent body, and the sin is taken up by the doer, for it is the fruit of his action."}},{"n":32,"text":"एवं संसारचक्रेऽस्मिन्व्याविद्धे रथचक्रवत् ।\nसमेति भूतग्रामोऽयं भूतग्रामेण कार्यवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So in this wheel of rebirth, turned like a chariot wheel, this host of beings meets another host of beings, each with its own purpose."}},{"n":33,"text":"जन्ममृत्युजराव्याधिवेदनाभिरुपद्रुतम् ।\nअसारमिममस्वन्तं संसारं त्यजतः सुखम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For one who gives up this worthless, endless cycle of rebirth, plagued by birth, death, old age, disease and pain, there is happiness."}},{"n":34,"text":"दिवः पतत्सु देवेषु स्थानेभ्यश्च महर्षिषु ।\nको हि नाम भवेनार्थी भवेत्कारणतत्त्ववित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When even the gods fall from heaven, and the great sages from their places, who that knows the truth of causes would not wish for freedom from becoming?"}},{"n":35,"text":"कृत्वा हि विविधं कर्म तत्तद्विविधलक्षणम् ।\nपार्थिवैर्नृपतिः स्वल्पैः कारणैरेव बध्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having done many kinds of deeds, each with its own marks, a king is bound by earthly things, by the smallest of causes."}},{"n":36,"text":"तस्मात्प्रज्ञामृतमिदं चिरान्मां प्रत्युपस्थितम् ।\nतत्प्राप्य प्रार्थये स्थानमव्ययं शाश्वतं ध्रुवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore this nectar of wisdom, which has come to me after a long time, I have reached, and I seek that imperishable, eternal, steady place."}},{"n":37,"text":"एतया सततं वृत्त्या चरन्नेवंप्रकारया ।\nदेहं संस्थापयिष्यामि निर्भयं मार्गमास्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Moving ever in this manner of life, I shall keep my body going, set on a fearless path."}}]}]}